---
import GuideContents from '../../components/shared/GuideContents.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/shared/PageIntro.astro';
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import { course } from '../../lib/course-data.js';
import { projectGuide } from '../../lib/server/project-guide.js';
import { siteUrl } from '../../lib/urls.js';

const content = projectGuide(
  { id: 'image-model-300m', source: 'projects/image-model-300m/TEACHING.md' },
  course,
);
const figureRoot = 'project-assets/image-model-300m/reference/evidence/v14/figures/';
---

<GuideLayout
  title="Flower image model: bounded CPU pilot and public evidence"
  description="Read the source-bound evidence from a short CPU image-model pilot, including its failed classification gate, staged training traces, retrieval results and seven reproducible figures."
  active="projects"
  skipLabel="Skip to the flower-model CPU pilot"
  mainClass="project-guide"
>
  <PageIntro
    backHref="project-plans/image-model-300m.html"
    backLabel="Full 300M image-model plan"
    edition="Optional workflow · bounded CPU pilot · quality gate failed"
    intro="Use this short flower-image run to learn how source freezes, staged objectives and public evidence fit together."
  >
    <Fragment slot="title" set:html={content.heading} />
    <p>
      The selected pilot classifier reached 0.318522 macro balanced accuracy, below its predeclared
      0.40 floor and the 0.363836 color control. Calibration and brightness checks passed, but the
      classification gate failed. The planned full 300M capstone remains Planned.
    </p>
    <p>
      This guide publishes source and numeric evidence for study. It does not include the photos,
      fitted weights or consumer package. A reader can review the public checks without downloading
      data or running training.
    </p>
    <p>
      The downloaded as-run README records the source-freeze pre-run state. Completed v14 outcomes
      are documented here and in the byte-exact TEACHING.md, with the exact receipt retained in the
      public packet.
    </p>
    <a class="button primary" href={siteUrl('downloads/image-model-300m-pilot.zip')} download>
      Download source and numeric evidence
    </a>
    <a class="button" href={siteUrl('project-plans/image-model-300m.html')}>
      Read the full capstone plan
    </a>
  </PageIntro>
  <aside
    class="material-status image-pilot-status"
    aria-label="Flower-model CPU pilot status"
    data-material-key="pilot:image-model-300m"
  >
    <p>
      <span class="material-badge" data-maturity="in-development">
        In development
      </span>
      <span> Source and numeric checks passed; the classification quality gate failed.</span>
    </p>
    <p>Teaching review pending.</p>
  </aside>
  <GuideContents
    sections={content.sections}
    label="Flower-model pilot sections"
    title="In this workflow"
  />
  <article set:html={content.body} />

  <section aria-labelledby="pilot-figures">
    <h2 id="pilot-figures">Seven public figures, with their units and limits</h2>
    <p>
      Every figure is rebuilt from the checked-in numeric packet. The loss objectives use different
      units, so compare each curve only within its own phase and objective.
    </p>

    <figure class="lesson-visual">
      <div class="figure-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable MAE loss figure">
        <a
          href={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}loss-mae.svg`)}
          aria-label="Open full-size figure: MAE masked reconstruction loss by one-based update, measured as mean squared normalized-pixel target."
          title="Open full-size figure: MAE masked reconstruction loss by one-based update, measured as mean squared normalized-pixel target."
        >
          <img
            src={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}loss-mae.svg`)}
            alt="MAE masked reconstruction loss by one-based update, measured as mean squared normalized-pixel target."
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        MAE falls across its local updates. Its y-axis is mean squared error on the selected
        normalized-pixel reconstruction targets, not classification loss.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="lesson-visual">
      <div class="figure-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable SimCLR loss figure">
        <a
          href={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}loss-simclr.svg`)}
          aria-label="Open full-size figure: SimCLR NT-Xent contrastive loss by one-based update, measured in nats per anchor."
          title="Open full-size figure: SimCLR NT-Xent contrastive loss by one-based update, measured in nats per anchor."
        >
          <img
            src={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}loss-simclr.svg`)}
            alt="SimCLR NT-Xent contrastive loss by one-based update, measured in nats per anchor."
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        SimCLR optimizes agreement between two augmented views. Read this curve in nats per anchor;
        its numeric scale is not comparable to the MAE or supervised curves.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="lesson-visual">
      <div class="figure-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable supervised loss figure">
        <a
          href={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}loss-supervised.svg`)}
          aria-label="Open full-size figure: Supervised cross-entropy by one-based update, measured in nats per example."
          title="Open full-size figure: Supervised cross-entropy by one-based update, measured in nats per example."
        >
          <img
            src={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}loss-supervised.svg`)}
            alt="Supervised cross-entropy by one-based update, measured in nats per example."
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        This is supervised cross-entropy in nats per example. The x-axis restarts at one for each
        phase, so it does not show one continuous training history.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="lesson-visual">
      <div class="figure-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable classification quality figure">
        <a
          href={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}quality-classification.svg`)}
          aria-label="Open full-size figure: Final macro balanced accuracy for the selected baseline ViT and fixed color-centroid control, with the predeclared 0.40 floor."
          title="Open full-size figure: Final macro balanced accuracy for the selected baseline ViT and fixed color-centroid control, with the predeclared 0.40 floor."
        >
          <img
            src={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}quality-classification.svg`)}
            alt="Final macro balanced accuracy for the selected baseline ViT and fixed color-centroid control, with the predeclared 0.40 floor."
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        The selected baseline ViT scores 0.318522 and the fixed color control scores 0.363836. Both
        are below the 0.40 floor, so the pilot classification result fails its gate.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="lesson-visual">
      <div class="figure-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable brightness robustness figure">
        <a
          href={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}quality-brightness.svg`)}
          aria-label="Open full-size figure: Balanced accuracy before and after a brightness increase, with the allowed maximum drop."
          title="Open full-size figure: Balanced accuracy before and after a brightness increase, with the allowed maximum drop."
        >
          <img
            src={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}quality-brightness.svg`)}
            alt="Balanced accuracy before and after a brightness increase, with the allowed maximum drop."
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        A brightness increase lowers balanced accuracy by 0.024903, within the declared 0.15 maximum
        drop. This robustness pass does not change the failed classification result.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="lesson-visual">
      <div class="figure-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable calibration figure">
        <a
          href={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}quality-calibration.svg`)}
          aria-label="Open full-size figure: Raw and development-temperature-calibrated final negative log likelihood against the allowed degradation."
          title="Open full-size figure: Raw and development-temperature-calibrated final negative log likelihood against the allowed degradation."
        >
          <img
            src={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}quality-calibration.svg`)}
            alt="Raw and development-temperature-calibrated final negative log likelihood against the allowed degradation."
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        The development-selected temperature is 1.020172. Calibrated final NLL is 1.508793 versus
        1.508965 raw, within the 0.05 degradation limit.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="lesson-visual">
      <div class="figure-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable retrieval figure">
        <a
          href={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}quality-retrieval.svg`)}
          aria-label="Open full-size figure: Final retrieval mAP for four representation arms over 547 queries."
          title="Open full-size figure: Final retrieval mAP for four representation arms over 547 queries."
        >
          <img
            src={siteUrl(`${figureRoot}quality-retrieval.svg`)}
            alt="Final retrieval mAP for four representation arms over 547 queries."
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Selected retrieval mAP is 0.234651 across 547 final queries. The public ranked IDs and class
        and component labels allow this value to be reconstructed without publishing embeddings.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
